                "reply_count": 369,
                "retweet_count": 86,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "For months, I have been clear: If you want my vote, we have to do something to address the cost of health care. We can open the government today with a simple, one-year extension of https://t.co/Qfch7PlgNa subsidies to keep Michiganders' health care from spiking before Jan 1.\n\nAnd once the government opens up, we can work in a bipartisan basis on the needed reforms for any future extensions.\n\nPresident Trump and Republicans should take the deal.  And if not, please come back with an offer that addresses the cost of health care.",
